Easy Problem :)

Easy to get that  $$ 2^n \equiv \begin{cases}
2  & \text{ if } n \text{ odd} 
1  & \text{ if } n \text{ even}
\end{cases}  $$  so it's easy to get the answer  $\boxed{n\equiv 1,2 \mod 6}$ .

Let  $A'$  the reflection of  $A$  over  $BC$ . It is easy to see that  $B,D,A'$  are collinear, therefore   $$ [A'BC]=[ABC]=[BPCD]\implies [PBC]=[A'CD] $$  Next, observe that  $\angle PCB=\angle DCA'$  (since  $\angle ACP=\angle BCD$ ). Now compute the areas of the triangles:
\begin{align*}
&[PBC]=\frac{1}{2}\cdot PC\cdot BC\cdot \sin(\angle PCB)=\frac{1}{2}\cdot DC\cdot A'C\cdot \sin(\angle DCA')=[A'CD][.2cm]
&\implies PC\cdot BC=DC\cdot A'C=DC\cdot AC\implies \frac{PC}{AC}=\frac{DC}{BC}
\end{align*}
Combining this with the equal angles  $\angle ACP=\angle BCD$  we deduce that  $\triangle BCD\sim \triangle ACP$ .

